  "_meta": {
    "about": "Supervisor editable access policy. Guests may chat and get public information; anything that needs customer data is blocked for guests. Edit this file and save: it is reloaded automatically when its modified time changes. A broken file is ignored and the last good policy stays in force.",
    "keyword_rules": "Keywords are matched against text normalized with NFC, casefold, collapsed whitespace and with zero width joiners removed. A keyword that starts with a Latin letter or digit only matches at a word start, and only to a word end unless it ends with an asterisk (bill* matches bills and billing). Sinhala and Tamil script keywords are matched as plain substrings because those languages attach endings to words. Latin letter Sinhala (Singlish) is listed under si and Latin letter Tamil (Tanglish) under ta.",
    "overrides": "public_overrides are regular expressions for general information questions. The matched part is removed from the text before the topic rules run, so 'how do I pay online' stays allowed but 'how do I pay online and what is my balance' is still blocked.",
    "language_note": "The Sinhala and Tamil keywords (script and Latin letters) and the Sinhala and Tamil built in replies are machine written. They need a review by a native speaker before production use."
  },
